# Godot 4 and GDScript Rules

- Target Godot 4.x, GDScript, and the Compatibility renderer. Avoid C# and proprietary extensions.
- Write code, comments, and documentation in English. Chat may be in Norwegian.
- Keep GUI and CLI presentation separate from game logic. Both call `scripts/core/`.
- Core must not import Control, SceneTree, UI components, stdin, or stdout.
- Use Custom Resources for game data and strongly typed, focused GDScript.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` for agent roles, verification, documentation, and task workflow.
- Read `docs/ProjectDescription.md` before architectural decisions and keep `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` aligned with implemented behavior.
- Use `docs/README.md` as the current task index. Work on the first unchecked task in the selected active backlog unless the user selects another task or section.
- Complete and verify one task at a time; update its owning backlog before moving on. Archived records preserve history and do not select active work.
- Test refactoring before and after changes. Run the existing checks for builds.
- Put session-only generated files, logs, and screenshots under ignored `localtmp/`.
